      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "We comment here because we seem to be able to identify the cause. First of all this happens on all uploaded models. I have investigated and found that the parameters of the hand gesture are not reflected to other players during the emote, but only affect me locally. I think this bug occurs because the parameters immediately before the emote remain as information to the surrounding players, and these parameters are maintained until the emote is released.\n\nThis bug only occurs with hand gesture parameters, so if you control the parameters from the normal EX menu and change the facial expression, it will still work during the emote.\n\nYou can take advantage of the fact that your own hand gesture parameters work correctly locally even during emotes, and you can force a solution by creating another layer and another parameter to refer to the hand gesture parameters in the FX layer and change the facial expression again, but it is not ideal. However, this is not ideal.\n\nI assume that this is because the hand gesture parameters are fixed at the moment the emote is started and are not reflected globally afterwards.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "64ef168ec9b209d6f6c56032",
