      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5e877e5e60de627e6ba7946a|full_name}: the problem isn't about the animation, layer or controller. The parameters GestureLeft and GestureRight are not being synced between remote users when you have an active emote (VRCEmote > 0), so independent of your setup, they're only being updated for you. \n\nHere is another video showing the issue: https://youtu.be/iptptDuz1-E\n\nAvatar ID: avtr_b62d2faf-b163-4821-a785-cf9026ac6bc6\n\n(I was pressing Shift+F2, if you want to know) \n\nSadly that avatar only have one or two expressions but should be enough to check. You can also check this with almost any 3.0 avatar, just need to be \"lucky\" to find one that didn't make any temporary workaround to deal with the issue (You can use the original parameters GestureLeft and GestureRight only locally to intermediate other synced parameters that will represent them and do their job, it works).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
